    "wikipedia_summary": "<i><b>Utricularia vulgaris</b></i> (<b>greater bladderwort</b> or <b>common bladderwort</b>) is an aquatic species of bladderwort found in Asia and Europe. The plant is free-floating and does not put down roots. Stems can attain lengths of over one metre in a single growing season, but die back and form turions in winter. The leaves are finely pinnately divided, between one and eight centimetres long and carry many bladder-like traps. The yellow flowers are borne on stalks above the surface...",
